Next-Gen Sécurité — hardened public webhooks, RLS invariants, CSP report,
E2EE tamper tests, and a ratcheted inventory gate

Task #768 is a cross-cutting epic. This commit delivers concrete runtime
hardening on the highest-risk surfaces and the automation that keeps the
remaining gap from growing. Edge-function consolidation (#226) and full
classification of the 186 remaining functions are tracked as follow-up
#772; this change makes regression on those impossible.

Runtime hardening (code changes)
- _shared/webhook-signature.ts (new): verifyHmacSha256 + constantTimeEqual
  backed by node:crypto timingSafeEqual.
- command-email-intake: HMAC-SHA-256 over raw body + constant-time legacy
  secret fallback; withRateLimit 60/min.
- command-approval-webhook: constant-time x-internal-secret compare;
  withRateLimit 120/min.
- receive-email: constant-time compare + withRateLimit 120/min;
  config.toml verify_jwt=false added.
- command-monitoring-cron: constant-time compare; verify_jwt=false.
- public-api: withRateLimit 120/min.
- csp-report (new function) + security_csp_reports table with RLS locked
  to service_role; wired into inventory manifest.

RLS invariants (DB)
- 20260419000000_rls_invariants.sql: creates system.rls_whitelist +
  system.assert_rls_invariants() + system.rls_audit_log. Checks every
  table in sensitive schemas has row_security enabled AND ≥1 policy
  (or an explicit whitelist row with a documented reason). Runs at
  migration time and records any violation. The "raise warning" stops
  short of breaking deploys today; upgraded to exception once the
  RLS audit backlog reaches zero.

E2EE (client)
- src/lib/__tests__/orbit-double-ratchet.test.ts: AES-GCM ciphertext
  tamper, IV tamper, and MAX_SKIP forged-header tests (5 tests, pass).

Deterministic inventory gate
- supabase/functions/_manifest.ts: ground-truth classification (38 entries).
- scripts/security-inventory-edge-functions.ts: cross-checks manifest vs
  config.toml vs handler source, exits non-zero on mismatches (exit 2)
  AND on unclassified-count regressions (exit 3). Baseline committed to
  docs/security/unclassified-baseline.json; ratchet only moves down.

CI (.github/workflows/security-audit.yml)
- dependency-audit: npm audit --audit-level=high on prod deps.
- sast: Semgrep p/owasp-top-ten + p/javascript + p/typescript + p/react
  (severity ERROR).
- secret-scan-weekly: belt-and-braces scan.
- edge-functions-inventory: runs the gate + enforces baseline file drift.
- e2ee-tests: runs the double-ratchet tamper + MAX_SKIP suite.

Documentation
- next-gen-security-hardening.md, owasp-top10-checklist.md,
  rls-audit-checklist.md, e2ee-orbit-audit.md, secrets-rotation.md,
  regenerated edge-functions-auth-inventory.md, unclassified-baseline.json.

Deviations
- 186 functions remain unclassified — ratcheted baseline prevents
